{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564707-m20-sorcerer-summoning-binding-warding-rules","id":1564707,"title":"M20: Sorcerer Summoning/Binding/Warding Rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-10-12T12:20:15-07:00","id":1564707,"title":"M20: Sorcerer Summoning/Binding/Warding Rules","content":"So, I thought I had a clear understanding of how the the Summoning/Binding/Warding (S/B/W) rules worked as they have been pretty consistent from second edition till the current M20 edition. I have entered into a minor dispute with my ST who feels you cannot summon without binding or warding first and that all three are needed. He is new to M20: Sorcerers and is still learning so I do not fault him for being confused. I explained that is not the case and the path is essentially three separate &quot;paths&quot; combined into one. Here is how I have always understood the rules: Let us use the example of dealing with a regular Mortal. Each method is its own ritual; there is a Summon Mortal ritual, Bind Mortal ritual, and Ward Against Mortal ritual. A sorcerer can perform any one of these rituals separately without doing the others. A sorcerer can choose to summon forth a mortal to their location, they can perform a ritual to bind a mortal to their service depending on the binding intensity of the aspect, and they can also ward themselves or an area against mortals. The sorcerer can do any one of these independently of the other.<br /> <br /> The dispute occurred because my sorcerer, a member of the Ancient Order of the Aeon Rites, has 3 dots in S/B/W and it is his affinity path. I plan for him to specialize in dealing with High Umbral entities. He knows the Summon Dominion 3 dot ritual. His paradigm states that binding High Umbral Angels or Celestial entities is egotistical and against the Sacred Equation of I AM. He therefore only summons forth these beings and then bargains with them to perform a service for him in exchange for performing a service for them. He recently summoned forth a Dominion, whose true name is Hadriel according to the Book of Aeon, to protect him and provide healing as he and the cabal of mages he is with get out of a skyscraper full of humans possessed by wraiths. He felt summoning his Guardian Angel Najayben, which is a rank 1 summoning ritual, would not be powerful enough to protect him from such a horde for long.<br /> <br /> The ST felt I could not summon Hardiel without performing the warding ritual and binding ritual. But I explained that my sorcerer never uses a warding circle or binding ritual when he deals with High Umbral entities and per RAW, I can perform the summoning without them. I then bargain, using M20s How Do You Do That?, bargaining rules, to come to a mutual agreement. I argued that he only does not need to bargain with Najayben because it is his &quot;Guardian Angel&quot; and it desires to help him to the best of its abilities within the scope of its duties. Of course, if he ever summoned forth a middle or low umbra entity, or a High Umbra demon, then he would use wards and a binding ritual given the nature of those entities.<br /> <br /> So, what is the correct assumption in this matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","user":"Starcomet","date":". 10-12-2026, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-12T15:33:48-07:00","id":1564710,"title":"","content":"M20: Sorcerer is pretty clear on this, too:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All Summoning, Binding, and Warding magics are rituals, and rituals exist for reaching individual beings or classes of beings. There are separate rituals to sum\u00admon, bind, and ward each target. [...] Though summoning a being may intrigue it, attempting to bind them tends to incur hostility, and magicians who either don\u2019t know or fail at casting the warding ritual often find themselves in a great deal of trouble. </div> </div> </div>S/B/W is always an act of compulsion (as opposed to Ephemera) and the Sorcerer needs to weigh whether binding would anger an entity they might want to summon again in the future, or worse, which may be powerful enough to come after them for revenge. It's essential that all rituals can be cast independent of each other, for this and other reasons - they may want to lay a ward as a precaution or bind a rogue entity they didn't summon, too. A personal guardian angel would probably feel very slighted if the Sorcerer were to ward against or bind them.<br /> <br /> Finding the right balance between precaution, respect, and diplomacy is probably the hardest aspect of the Path imo, but also what makes it interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-13T05:24:07-07:00","id":1564719,"title":"","content":"I decided to bow out of their game. Our interpretation of the path's grey areas did not align. I feel a high umbral &quot;angel&quot; entity would not be inherently hostile just for summoning them. Especially if the sorcerer or mage is humble and following protocol and not trying to bind them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-13T07:30:09-07:00","id":1564720,"title":"","content":"So I don't have M20 Sorcerer but it sounds like you have the right of it that you can summon without binding or warding. They certainly are different effects with awakened magic because there are actually two levels of summoning. A mage can call out to a spirit at Rank 2 of Spirit, though it doesn't have to answer if it doesn't want to, and he can compel a spirit to come at Spirit 4.<br /> <br /> Now I sort of get why your former ST might have been confused. There's a classic vision of a mage first setting up a binding circle and then summoning a demon into it, and it is easy to see how someone might assume that the binding is a fundamental necessity of the summoning rather than something a wise mage does before summoning a demon. It's a bit of confirmation bias, really. The mages who summon demons without protecting themselves don't tend to stick around long enough to tell their stories. How Do You Do That says pretty much the same thing, which is strong corroboration that it is possible to summon without Warding or Binding.<br /> <br /> But just because some entities are dangerous to summon without binding doesn't mean that all of them are, or that binding is always a good idea, particularly in this case. You've set out a good case for the kind of entities you are looking to deal with and the basics of how they act and react. Or to put it another way, you've made a request that certain elements important to your character be incorporated into the game world. That's generally an opportunity for an ST to work with the player and get them invested in the game and the world. Ignoring that over a dispute in mechanics is a missed opportunity. <br /> <br /> Anyways, it sounds like this was an important enough element of your gameplay that dropping out of the game was the right call. I hope you find a group that matches your playstyle better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-13T09:49:04-07:00","id":1564724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564707-m20-sorcerer-summoning-binding-warding-rules?p=1564720#post1564720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I don't have M20 Sorcerer but it sounds like you have the right of it that you can summon without binding or warding. They certainly are different effects with awakened magic because there are actually two levels of summoning. A mage can call out to a spirit at Rank 2 of Spirit, though it doesn't have to answer if it doesn't want to, and he can compel a spirit to come at Spirit 4.<br /> <br /> Now I sort of get why your former ST might have been confused. There's a classic vision of a mage first setting up a binding circle and then summoning a demon into it, and it is easy to see how someone might assume that the binding is a fundamental necessity of the summoning rather than something a wise mage does before summoning a demon. It's a bit of confirmation bias, really. The mages who summon demons without protecting themselves don't tend to stick around long enough to tell their stories. How Do You Do That says pretty much the same thing, which is strong corroboration that it is possible to summon without Warding or Binding.<br /> <br /> But just because some entities are dangerous to summon without binding doesn't mean that all of them are, or that binding is always a good idea, particularly in this case. You've set out a good case for the kind of entities you are looking to deal with and the basics of how they act and react. Or to put it another way, you've made a request that certain elements important to your character be incorporated into the game world. That's generally an opportunity for an ST to work with the player and get them invested in the game and the world. Ignoring that over a dispute in mechanics is a missed opportunity.<br /> <br /> Anyways, it sounds like this was an important enough element of your gameplay that dropping out of the game was the right call. I hope you find a group that matches your playstyle better.</div> </div> </div> </div>He had indicated he is 100% RAW and M20 resources only. But he admitted he was new to M20:Sorcerer as he has only ever ran with Mage characters. I had hoped he would allow this as it is a grey area and does not break RAW, but he was adamant that since the book does not say it, I cannot do it. He for example said I could not summon a specific named being even if I had their True Name because the mechanics did not specified that. It would always be a random generic angel/high umbral entity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-13T12:29:32-07:00","id":1564727,"title":"","content":"All I can say is good luck to him trying to run Mage 20th 100% RAW. There's entire rules that are missing or contradictory and a large chunk of the given sphere requirements don't make sense. It's even worse in How Do You Do That?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-13T19:04:20-07:00","id":1564736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starcomet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564707-m20-sorcerer-summoning-binding-warding-rules?p=1564724#post1564724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He had indicated he is 100% RAW and M20 resources only. But he admitted he was new to M20:Sorcerer as he has only ever ran with Mage characters. I had hoped he would allow this as it is a grey area and does not break RAW, but he was adamant that since the book does not say it, I cannot do it. He for example said I could not summon a specific named being even if I had their True Name because the mechanics did not specified that. It would always be a random generic angel/high umbral entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand the sentiment, but it's a bad idea in any RPG and a hundred fold so in Mage.<br /> <br /> What probably happens isn't even that they're 100% RAW, but they're 100% convinced the version of the game in their head is RAW and inviolable.<br /> <br /> This type is usually extremely bad to deal with anyone outside their main group, and even with those tend to drive them away with time. It's a shame, but I don't think you'll get anything out of this ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-14T06:42:53-07:00","id":1564745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564707-m20-sorcerer-summoning-binding-warding-rules?p=1564736#post1564736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can understand the sentiment, but it's a bad idea in any RPG and a hundred fold so in Mage.<br /> <br /> What probably happens isn't even that they're 100% RAW, but they're 100% convinced the version of the game in their head is RAW and inviolable.<br /> <br /> This type is usually extremely bad to deal with anyone outside their main group, and even with those tend to drive them away with time. It's a shame, but I don't think you'll get anything out of this ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>As evidence, contrast the ruling that sorcerers can't summon specific entities because the mechanics don't say they can with the quote from the book that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> posted: &quot;All Summoning, Binding, and Warding magics are rituals, and rituals exist for reaching <u>individual beings</u> or classes of beings.&quot; It is an obvious and reasonable interpretation of that text that specific individuals are possible, so by RAW it should be allowed.<br /> <br /> Now 'you can summon a random individual of a type' also matches those words, but it is much less obvious and much less reasonable interpretation. Playing that way is much less <i>Read as Written</i> and much more <i>Guess How I'm Reading What is Written</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-14T09:44:05-07:00","id":1564747,"title":"","content":"I think the Path was initially designed with mainly Faustian bargains in mind, a situation in which you certainly want to employ all three aspects (and be a lawyer that is immune to double-speak). That still shines through the phrasing in S20, and I can see why someone would assume that narrow scope after only skip reading. Still, even in these situations you would want to summon Mephistopheles, and not Random Demon No. 291.<br /> <br /> I just checked 1e Sorcerer, and even there it's optional whether to use any single aspect of S/B/W or not. And while the Path mainly talks about generic summonings, the rules state that calling on individuals is also possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-14T14:29:44-07:00","id":1564752,"title":"","content":"M20 Sorcerer developer here. You can absolutely summon a specific entity. You can barter with that entity just like any other being. Binding is only required if you want to compel the being's aid or force a task. Warding is only required to protect yourself from said entity. Regardless they are separate rituals.<br /> <br /> However, the Storyteller could certainly rule that if you have no established relationship with a being (i.e., you've not already interacted in game, and you didn't spend Background dots to represent them) that entity can react as friendly or unfriendly as they deem appropriate in a given scene. I personally see angels as horrific monsters who turn cities to salt and tend to find humanity annoying, so I'd personally make those interactions rough, at least at first. And binding anything without a ward is a recipe for getting your face eaten.<br /> <br /> In any case I'm sorry to hear you had that experience, but it also sounds like you made the right call by leaving","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-15T07:50:22-07:00","id":1564759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564707-m20-sorcerer-summoning-binding-warding-rules?p=1564752#post1564752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20 Sorcerer developer here. You can absolutely summon a specific entity. You can barter with that entity just like any other being. Binding is only required if you want to compel the being's aid or force a task. Warding is only required to protect yourself from said entity. Regardless they are separate rituals.<br /> <br /> However, the Storyteller could certainly rule that if you have no established relationship with a being (i.e., you've not already interacted in game, and you didn't spend Background dots to represent them) that entity can react as friendly or unfriendly as they deem appropriate in a given scene. I personally see angels as horrific monsters who turn cities to salt and tend to find humanity annoying, so I'd personally make those interactions rough, at least at first. And binding anything without a ward is a recipe for getting your face eaten.<br /> <br /> In any case I'm sorry to hear you had that experience, but it also sounds like you made the right call by leaving</div> </div> </div> </div>I fully agree binding anything without a ward is foolish! And I also agree that angels, and many high umbra entities, are fearsome beings and I always treat them as such. I indicated in my backstory he had a good relations with his guardian angel and it is why he had his True Name. The only mechanical tie in with my background was my 5 dot Spiritual Relic/Artifact that was given to him by his Guardian Angel. <br /> <br /> I had hoped that was enough to make other angels be at least intrigued to hear my offer when I summoned them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-15T08:01:15-07:00","id":1564760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starcomet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564707-m20-sorcerer-summoning-binding-warding-rules?p=1564759#post1564759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had hoped that was enough to make other angels be at least intrigued to hear my offer when I summoned them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really a table call, tbh. Something to establish during session zero. I totally understand why you'd want that to be the case, but I can also see why a Storyteller may want to put restrictions on it. I do *not* see why they wouldn't let you just summon them and leave it to roleplaying and maybe the dice to determine how the angels react, but I wasn't at the table either. In any case, I hope you can find a table that better suits the experience you're looking for!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-15T09:04:58-07:00","id":1564761,"title":"","content":"I the situation as a missed opportunity. Character concepts are a way the player tells the ST how and where they want to interact with the game. More often than not they are an opportunity to work together to build up the world and get player investment. If the ST doesn't have that part of the world development, now he has someone to brainstorm that with. If he does have that part developed, now he has a player who is in on some of the knowledge and can act as a source of information for the rest. Depending on the player he can even outsource some of the ST work.<br /> <br /> And even if the character concept is truly incompatible with the structure of the chronicle, there's still the opportunity to discuss why and what changes could make it work. Even if the player isn't interested in making those changes, at least he will have some indication of why the concept doesn't work.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}